{
 "alias_version": "2.0",
 "note": "Canonical space aliases. Matching is normalise -> EXACT -> TOKEN/PHRASE, unique match required; two different canonical labels matching is AMBIGUOUS, zero is UNKNOWN. There is NO substring mode: 'room' sits inside BEDROOM, MAID_ROOM, IRON_ROOM and SERVICE_ROOM. The raw drawing label is never destroyed. EXACT means 'exactly and nothing else' and is reserved for the dangerous generics; every alias can still match a whole normalised string. A dangerous generic (room, hall, area, service, غرفة, صالة) is held as LEGACY_ONLY: it is recorded but can never classify a space alone. 'صالة طعام' still resolves, because the phrase carries the meaning the bare word does not.",
 "dangerous_generics": [
  "room",
  "hall",
  "area",
  "service",
  "غرفة",
  "صالة",
  "صاله"
 ],
